attr[seg_0000:274a]: type = code; name = vm_branch_take; comment = [[[
    Takes a relative branch -- `add ax, si` applies the displacement to the program counter. Also carries the task bookkeeping: a stack at ss:[0c56] and a frame slot at es:[bp-0ch], so scripts can be suspended and resumed.
]]]
attr[seg_0000:26eb]: type = code; name = vm_run; comment = [[[
    The statement interpreter -- the outer loop of the script VM.
        sub ah,ah / lodsb / add ax,ax / mov bx,ax / call cs:[bx+24h] / jmp back
    So an opcode is a byte, the table is WORD-scaled (base image 0x24, 231 entries,
    opcodes 0..230 -- every value, not just even), and handlers are CALLed, which is why
    they end in `ret`. The expression table at 01f2 is byte-scaled instead, so its opcodes
    really are even; the two tables do not share a convention. FORMATS.md section 6.
]]]
attr[seg_0000:0024]: type = u16; name = vm_statement_table; comment = [[[
    231 handler pointers, image 0x24..0x1f2, indexed as 0x24 + opcode*2 by vm_run.
    Statements, control flow and the engine primitives all live here. Opcodes 0..4 point
    at 26f9..26fd, which are single `ret` bytes -- no-ops.
]]]

// Statement/primitive signatures, generated from vm_statement_table (T29).
